[SIZE="4"][B]Inventory Companion Changelog[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE="2"][B]Unreleased[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Upgraded saved-variable schema to version 3 before loading profiles, preserving existing settings and protecting shared DEV/release data from incompatible older builds. Older schema 2 builds refuse the upgraded data; downgrading requires restoring a compatible backup with the game closed.
[*]Replaced the item editor's separate Group/Totals toggles with aligned two-line Show and Notify controls that open compact checkbox boxes. Details summarize selected settings; None retains the existing inactive coloring.
[*]Added independent backpack and bank display choices, including bank-only counts, and separate Chat/HUD pickup notification destinations. Existing preferences inherit their previous behavior.
[*]Notification destinations combine requests from individually tracked items and matching groups without duplicating each gain. Notifications remain active when the tracker is hidden; burst suppression never redirects to a destination you disabled.
[*]Editor flag changes and removal reject obsolete row/profile targets. Checkbox boxes close on click-away, scrolling, or editor changes, and rebind safely after edits.
[*]Added Include/Exclude controls to group pattern rows. A green deposit (IN) or red withdraw (OUT) status icon identifies the current kind, and a compact swap button changes it; hover for explanations. Exclusions narrow only their own group, and existing patterns remain Includes.
[*]Group pattern rows are organized with Includes first and Excludes below a divider; changing a row's kind moves it to the matching section.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.5.0[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Fixed automatically sized tracker groups reopening after you deliberately closed them. Closed groups now stay closed across inventory changes, settings changes, and UI reloads until you open them again.
[*]Automatic height-related collapses are now temporary and no longer overwrite your saved group preferences. Groups you prefer open can return when space permits.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.4.1[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Groups with more than 200 eligible items now show an overflow message instead of constructing a large list of item rows. Narrow the group's patterns to display its items; summary counts still include all matching items.
[*]Added an amber information icon to oversized groups. Groups with up to 200 eligible items retain their normal item rows and scrolling.
[*]Removed an unwanted debug chat message when the tracking editors reposition the tracker panel.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.4.0 [Unreleased][/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.3.2[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Refined tracker scrolling so the panel keeps a fixed width, with item names narrowed and counts shifted left only while a scrollbar is visible.
[*]Fixed empty group patterns so they no longer match every item.
[*]Fixed tiny text in group pattern fields and editor search boxes when AddonSelector is not loaded. These fields now use a standard ESO font.
[*]Added Maximum Visible Rows to the Item Tracker Panel settings. The tracker uses single-line names before collapsing categories, and scrolls when the remaining content cannot fit. The title and edit button stay visible.
[*]Opening a category leaves other categories unchanged when they fit; otherwise, the other categories collapse. If all categories fit expanded, the tracker can open them automatically.
[*]Inventory updates that overflow the panel keep the single growing category open if it was already expanded; otherwise, categories collapse. Expansion and collapse choices are remembered.
[*]Added a Tracker Title Size setting with a regular-weight font and a matching edit icon. Item-row text and icons are unchanged.
[*]Added an assignable Show/Hide Item Tracking Panel keybinding and an Open Item Tracking Editor button on the main Inventory Companion addon settings page.
[*]Fixed item names overlapping their counts on the initial tracker render, and made single-line ellipses match item quality colors.
[*]Added a settings button beside the tracker title's edit button to open Inventory Companion's Add-on Settings page directly.
[*]The tracker visibility toggle now hides the panel in inventory, bank, and editor windows too, instead of leaving a visible panel with updates disabled.
[*]Added an Other Settings button beside the title in both tracking editors to return directly to Inventory Companion's Add-on Settings page.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.2.1[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Improved the built-in diagnostic report and performance checks.
[/LIST]

Bank transfers, item tracking, currency notifications, and settings work as before.

[SIZE="2"][B]1.01[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Maintenance update with no changes to everyday features.
[/LIST]

[SIZE="2"][B]1.00[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*]Initial release with crafted-item bank transfers, house-chest stack merging, item and group tracking, and currency and inventory-capacity panels.
[/LIST]
